IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`
IMPORT `s121-support`

-- 26 U.S.C. section 121. LAYER 1, module 5: subsections (d)(1) to (d)(8), the special rules.
-- Rules that "include" or "treat as" return the periods they add as a MAYBE list: JUST the periods when the rule's condition holds,
-- NOTHING ("limited by its own wording") when it does not. A caller that wants the periods adds none for NOTHING.
-- Borrowed terms are inputs: sections 216, 267(b), 707(b), 1033, 1041(a) and 1250(b)(3) are not among the sources.

§ `Subsection (d)(1): joint returns`

-- src:67 | (1) Joint returns
-- src:68 | If a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange of the property, subsections (a) and (c) shall apply if either spouse meets the ownership and use requirements of subsection (a) with respect to such property.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(1) (src:67-68)
GIVEN `a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first spouse meets the ownership and use requirements` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the second spouse meets the ownership and use requirements` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(1) subsections (a) and (c) apply to the joint return` MEANS
    IF `a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange`
    THEN `either is true` `the first spouse meets the ownership and use requirements` `the second spouse meets the ownership and use requirements`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange of the property" -- not a joint return is outside the provision's scope (fork F12: failed "if" at the chapeau, read as scope)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Subsection (d)(2): property of deceased spouse`

-- src:69 | (2) Property of deceased spouse
-- src:70 | For purposes of this section, in the case of an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of the sale or exchange of property, the period such unmarried individual owned and used such property shall include the period such deceased spouse owned and used such property before death.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(2), periods of ownership (src:69-70)
GIVEN `an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of the sale or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased spouse's periods of ownership` IS A LIST OF Span
      `the date of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Span)
`s 121(d)(2) the periods the deceased spouse owned the property before death are included` MEANS
    IF `an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of the sale or exchange`
    THEN JUST (`the spans up to and including` `the deceased spouse's periods of ownership` (`the date with day number` (`the day number of` `the date of death` MINUS 1)))
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of the sale or exchange of property"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:69 | (2) Property of deceased spouse
-- src:70 | For purposes of this section, in the case of an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of the sale or exchange of property, the period such unmarried individual owned and used such property shall include the period such deceased spouse owned and used such property before death.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(2), periods of use (src:69-70)
GIVEN `an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of the sale or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased spouse's periods of use as the principal residence` IS A LIST OF Span
      `the date of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Span)
`s 121(d)(2) the periods the deceased spouse used the property before death are included` MEANS
    IF `an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of the sale or exchange`
    THEN JUST (`the spans up to and including` `the deceased spouse's periods of use as the principal residence` (`the date with day number` (`the day number of` `the date of death` MINUS 1)))
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of the sale or exchange of property"
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Subsection (d)(3): property owned by spouse or former spouse`

-- src:73 | (A) Property transferred to individual from spouse or former spouse
-- src:74 | In the case of an individual holding property transferred to such individual in a transaction described in section 1041(a), the period such individual owns such property shall include the period the transferor owned the property.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(3)(A) (src:73-74)
GIVEN `holding property transferred in a transaction described in section 1041(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferor's periods of ownership` IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Span)
`s 121(d)(3)(A) the period the transferor owned the property is included` MEANS
    IF `holding property transferred in a transaction described in section 1041(a)`
    THEN JUST `the transferor's periods of ownership`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of an individual holding property transferred to such individual in a transaction described in section 1041(a)" (section 1041(a) is outside the sources)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (C): the divorce or separation instrument. Three clauses, closed by "means".
-- src:79 | (i) a decree of divorce or separate maintenance or a written instrument incident to such a decree,
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(3)(C)(i) (src:79)
GIVEN instrument IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(3)(C)(i) the instrument is a decree of divorce or separate maintenance or a written instrument incident to such a decree` MEANS
    instrument's `a decree of divorce or separate maintenance` OR instrument's `a written instrument incident to such a decree`

-- src:80 | (ii) a written separation agreement, or
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(3)(C)(ii) (src:80)
GIVEN instrument IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(3)(C)(ii) the instrument is a written separation agreement` MEANS
    instrument's `a written separation agreement`

-- src:81 | (iii) a decree (not described in clause (i)) requiring a spouse to make payments for the support or maintenance of the other spouse.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(3)(C)(iii) (src:81)
GIVEN instrument IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(3)(C)(iii) the instrument is a decree not described in clause (i) requiring support payments` MEANS
        instrument's `a decree requiring a spouse to make payments for the support or maintenance of the other spouse`
    AND NOT (`s 121(d)(3)(C)(i) the instrument is a decree of divorce or separate maintenance or a written instrument incident to such a decree` instrument)

-- src:77 | (C) Divorce or separation instrument
-- src:78 | For purposes of this paragraph, the term “divorce or separation instrument” means—
-- src:79 | (i) a decree of divorce or separate maintenance or a written instrument incident to such a decree,
-- src:80 | (ii) a written separation agreement, or
-- src:81 | (iii) a decree (not described in clause (i)) requiring a spouse to make payments for the support or maintenance of the other spouse.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(3)(C) (src:77-81)
GIVEN instrument IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(3)(C) the instrument is a divorce or separation instrument` MEANS
    IF    `s 121(d)(3)(C)(i) the instrument is a decree of divorce or separate maintenance or a written instrument incident to such a decree` instrument
       OR `s 121(d)(3)(C)(ii) the instrument is a written separation agreement` instrument
       OR `s 121(d)(3)(C)(iii) the instrument is a decree not described in clause (i) requiring support payments` instrument
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the term “divorce or separation instrument” means— (i) ..., (ii) ..., or (iii) ..." (a "means" definition)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (B): treated as using the property while the spouse or former spouse is granted use, during any period of ownership.
-- src:75 | (B) Property used by former spouse pursuant to divorce decree, etc.
-- src:76 | Solely for purposes of this section, an individual shall be treated as using property as such individual’s principal residence during any period of ownership while such individual’s spouse or former spouse is granted use of the property under a divorce or separation instrument.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(3)(B) (src:75-76)
GIVEN `periods of ownership` IS A LIST OF Span
      `uses granted to a spouse or former spouse` IS A LIST OF `Use granted`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Span)
`s 121(d)(3)(B) the individual is treated as using the property as the principal residence while a spouse or former spouse is granted use` MEANS
    IF null grantsUnderAnInstrument
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during any period of ownership while such individual’s spouse or former spouse is granted use of the property under a divorce or separation instrument" -- no such grant, no deemed use.
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the spans common to both lists` `periods of ownership` (map (GIVEN g YIELD g's `days`) grantsUnderAnInstrument))
    WHERE
        grantsUnderAnInstrument MEANS filter (GIVEN g YIELD `s 121(d)(3)(C) the instrument is a divorce or separation instrument` (g's `instrument`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) `uses granted to a spouse or former spouse`

§ `Subsection (d)(4): tenant-stockholder in cooperative housing corporation`

-- src:83 | For purposes of this section, if the taxpayer holds stock as a tenant-stockholder (as defined in section 216) in a cooperative housing corporation (as defined in such section), then—
-- src:84 | (A) the holding requirements of subsection (a) shall be applied to the holding of such stock, and
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(4)(A) (src:83-84)
GIVEN `holds stock as a tenant-stockholder in a cooperative housing corporation (both as defined in section 216)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `periods of holding the stock` IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Span)
`s 121(d)(4)(A) the holding requirement is applied to the holding of the stock` MEANS
    IF `holds stock as a tenant-stockholder in a cooperative housing corporation (both as defined in section 216)`
    THEN JUST `periods of holding the stock`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the taxpayer holds stock as a tenant-stockholder (as defined in section 216) in a cooperative housing corporation (as defined in such section)" (section 216 is outside the sources)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:83 | For purposes of this section, if the taxpayer holds stock as a tenant-stockholder (as defined in section 216) in a cooperative housing corporation (as defined in such section), then—
-- src:84 | (A) the holding requirements of subsection (a) shall be applied to the holding of such stock, and
-- src:85 | (B) the use requirements of subsection (a) shall be applied to the house or apartment which the taxpayer was entitled to occupy as such stockholder.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(4)(B) (src:83-85)
GIVEN `holds stock as a tenant-stockholder in a cooperative housing corporation (both as defined in section 216)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `periods of use of the house or apartment the taxpayer was entitled to occupy as stockholder` IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Span)
`s 121(d)(4)(B) the use requirement is applied to the house or apartment the taxpayer was entitled to occupy` MEANS
    IF `holds stock as a tenant-stockholder in a cooperative housing corporation (both as defined in section 216)`
    THEN JUST `periods of use of the house or apartment the taxpayer was entitled to occupy as stockholder`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the taxpayer holds stock as a tenant-stockholder (as defined in section 216) in a cooperative housing corporation (as defined in such section)"
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Subsection (d)(5): involuntary conversions`

-- src:87 | (A) In general
-- src:88 | For purposes of this section, the destruction, theft, seizure, requisition, or condemnation of property shall be treated as the sale of such property.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(5)(A) (src:87-88)
GIVEN event IS AN `Event in respect of the property`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(5)(A) the event is treated as the sale of the property` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `destruction` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `theft` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `seizure` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `requisition` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `condemnation` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a sale or exchange is already a sale, and (d)(5)(A) says nothing about any other event.
    WHEN `sale or exchange` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list is not closed by "only", so another event is not said to be treated as a sale.
    WHEN `some other event` THEN NOTHING

-- src:89 | (B) Application of section 1033
-- src:90 | In applying section 1033 (relating to involuntary conversions), the amount realized from the sale or exchange of property shall be treated as being the amount determined without regard to this section, reduced by the amount of gain not included in gross income pursuant to this section.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(5)(B) (src:89-90)
GIVEN `the amount realized, determined without regard to this section` IS A NUMBER
      `the gain not included in gross income pursuant to this section` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(d)(5)(B) the amount realized in applying section 1033` MEANS
    `the amount realized, determined without regard to this section` MINUS `the gain not included in gross income pursuant to this section`

-- src:91 | (C) Property acquired after involuntary conversion
-- src:92 | If the basis of the property sold or exchanged is determined (in whole or in part) under section 1033(b) (relating to basis of property acquired through involuntary conversion), then the holding and use by the taxpayer of the converted property shall be treated as holding and use by the taxpayer of the property sold or exchanged.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(5)(C) (src:91-92)
GIVEN `the basis of the property sold is determined (in whole or in part) under section 1033(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the converted property's holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A MAYBE Holding
`s 121(d)(5)(C) the holding and use of the converted property are treated as holding and use of the property sold` MEANS
    IF `the basis of the property sold is determined (in whole or in part) under section 1033(b)`
    THEN JUST `the converted property's holding`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the basis of the property sold or exchanged is determined (in whole or in part) under section 1033(b)" (section 1033 is outside the sources)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Subsection (d)(6): recognition of gain attributable to depreciation`

-- May 6, 1997 is the text's own date. An adjustment counts when the period it is attributable to is after that date;
-- one wholly on or before it does not; one that straddles it is not covered, because the text does not say how to divide it.
-- src:93 | (6) Recognition of gain attributable to depreciation
-- src:94 | Subsection (a) shall not apply to so much of the gain from the sale of any property as does not exceed the portion of the depreciation adjustments (as defined in section 1250(b)(3)) attributable to periods after May 6, 1997, in respect of such property.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(6) (src:93-94)
GIVEN gain IS A NUMBER
      adjustments IS A LIST OF `Depreciation adjustment`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 121(d)(6) the gain to which subsection (a) shall not apply` MEANS
    IF any straddles adjustments
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks of adjustments "attributable to periods after May 6, 1997" and does not say how to divide one attributable to a period that begins on or before that date and ends after it.
    THEN NOTHING
    -- "Subsection (a) shall not apply to so much of the gain ... as does not exceed" the adjustments after May 6, 1997: that amount of the gain, or all of it if smaller.
    ELSE JUST (`the smaller of` gain (sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `amount`) (filter `is after May 6, 1997` adjustments))))
    WHERE
        `May 6, 1997` MEANS Date 6 5 1997
        `is after May 6, 1997` a MEANS `the day number of` (a's `period it is attributable to`'s `first day`) GREATER THAN `the day number of` `May 6, 1997`
        straddles a MEANS
                `the day number of` (a's `period it is attributable to`'s `first day`) AT MOST `the day number of` `May 6, 1997`
            AND `the day number of` (a's `period it is attributable to`'s `last day`) GREATER THAN `the day number of` `May 6, 1997`

§ `Subsection (d)(7): determination of use during periods of out-of-residence care`

-- src:95 | (7) Determination of use during periods of out-of-residence care
-- src:96 | In the case of a taxpayer who—
-- src:97 | (A) becomes physically or mentally incapable of self-care, and
-- src:98 | (B) owns property and uses such property as the taxpayer’s principal residence during the 5-year period described in subsection (a) for periods aggregating at least 1 year,
-- src:99 | then the taxpayer shall be treated as using such property as the taxpayer’s principal residence during any time during such 5-year period in which the taxpayer owns the property and resides in any facility (including a nursing home) licensed by a State or political subdivision to care for an individual in the taxpayer’s condition.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(7) (src:95-99)
GIVEN `the taxpayer becomes physically or mentally incapable of self-care` IS A BOOLEAN
      holding IS A Holding
      window IS A Span
      sale IS A DATE
      stays IS A LIST OF `Stay in a facility`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Span)
`s 121(d)(7) the taxpayer is treated as using the property as the principal residence while residing in a licensed facility` MEANS
    IF `the taxpayer becomes physically or mentally incapable of self-care`
         AND `the days both owned and used inside the window` AT LEAST `the days in the years ending on` sale 1
    THEN JUST (`the spans common to both lists` (`the spans common to both lists` (holding's `periods of ownership`) licensedStays) (LIST window))
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a taxpayer who— (A) becomes physically or mentally incapable of self-care, and (B) owns property and uses such property as the taxpayer’s principal residence during the 5-year period described in subsection (a) for periods aggregating at least 1 year"
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the days both owned and used inside the window` MEANS `the days in both lists inside the window` (holding's `periods of ownership`) (holding's `periods of use as the principal residence`) window
        licensedStays MEANS map (GIVEN st YIELD st's `days`) (filter (GIVEN st YIELD st's `facility licensed by a State or political subdivision to care for an individual in the taxpayer's condition`) stays)

§ `Subsection (d)(8): sales of remainder interests`

-- src:102 | (A) In general
-- src:103 | At the election of the taxpayer, this section shall not fail to apply to the sale or exchange of an interest in a principal residence by reason of such interest being a remainder interest in such residence, but this section shall not apply to any other interest in such residence which is sold or exchanged separately.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(8)(A) (src:102-103)
GIVEN `the interest sold is a remainder interest in the principal residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the taxpayer elects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest is another interest in the residence sold or exchanged separately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(8)(A) this section does not fail to apply to the sale of the interest by reason of its being a remainder interest` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the interest sold is a remainder interest in the principal residence` AND `the taxpayer elects` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the interest sold is a remainder interest in the principal residence` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is given "At the election of the taxpayer"; with no election the text is silent.
            NOTHING
        IF `the interest is another interest in the residence sold or exchanged separately` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section shall not apply to any other interest in such residence which is sold or exchanged separately"
            JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a sale of the whole residence is not one this subparagraph speaks of.
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:104 | (B) Exception for sales to related parties
-- src:105 | Subparagraph (A) shall not apply to any sale to, or exchange with, any person who bears a relationship to the taxpayer which is described in section 267(b) or 707(b).
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(8)(B) (src:104-105)
GIVEN `the sale is to, or the exchange is with, a person who bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in section 267(b) or 707(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(8)(B) subparagraph (A) applies to the sale` MEANS
    IF `the sale is to, or the exchange is with, a person who bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in section 267(b) or 707(b)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subparagraph (A) shall not apply to any sale to, or exchange with, any person who bears a relationship to the taxpayer which is described in section 267(b) or 707(b)." (a flat negative)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says only where (A) does not apply.
    ELSE NOTHING
